    {
      "id": "jtkzv8y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Parliament of India consists of the President, Lok Sabha (House of the People), and Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Articles 79 to 122 in Part V of the Constitution govern the composition, duration, procedures, and powers of Parliament.",
        "Lok Sabha represents the people directly through direct elections, while Rajya Sabha represents the states and Union Territories.",
        "Parliament holds diverse powers including Legislative, Financial, Executive Control, and Judicial functions.",
        "In cases of disagreement between both Houses on ordinary bills, a Joint Sitting is summoned under Article 108."
      ],
      "id": "f6z24e6"
    },
